.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VOP_MKDIR 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_mkdir
.Nd create a directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_mkdir "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vop_mkdir
function creates a new directory named
.Fa name
in the directory
.Fa dvp .
If successful, the new directory vnode is returned in
.Fa *vpp
with a reference count incremented.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa cred"
.It Fa dvp
The parent directory vnode.
.It Fa vpp
Pointer to a vnode pointer where the new directory vnode will be stored.
.It Fa cnp
The component name information for the new directory.
.It Fa vap
The attributes (including mode) for the new directory.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width ".Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP"
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The filesystem does not support this operation.
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
The vnode
.Fa dvp
is not a directory.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
The directory already exists.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_create 9
